ADDITIONAL NOTICE — this repository contains medical information

This repository is educational material. It is not medical advice, it does not
establish a clinician-patient relationship, and it must not be used to make
treatment decisions. See SAFETY.md.

Nothing in this repository replaces insulin. A person with Type 1 diabetes who
stops taking insulin develops diabetic ketoacidosis within 12 to 48 hours.

If you reuse this material, please carry SAFETY.md and the status labels with
it. The verdicts are what make the rest of it safe to read, and content
separated from them can mislead in exactly the way this repository exists to
prevent.
